petra 0

# Two adjustable regulators in a chain. An LM317 sets a 5 V rail with its 121 ohm and
# 365 ohm feedback pair, and an adjustable LDO takes 5 V down to 3.3 V with its own pair.
# Each output depends on its reference's spread, the adjust or feedback pin current and
# both resistors' tolerances. The LM317 also needs a minimum load to stay in regulation,
# and its own top resistor draws most of it. The claims bound both rails.

board power {
  supply vin voltage given voltage capacity given capacity
  regulator v5 part reg.lm317_to220 from vin top r1 bottom r2
  resistor r1 part res.0603_1pct value 121 ohm
  resistor r2 part res.0603_1pct value 365 ohm
  regulator v3 part reg.ldo_adj_sot23_5 from v5 top r3 bottom r4
  resistor r3 part res.0603_1pct value 16.9 kohm
  resistor r4 part res.0603_1pct value 10 kohm
  sink motor from v5
  sink mcu from v3
}
